text:
Title: encoding/json/v2: unmarshaling is rejected when an embedded type implements marshal methods

Body: ### Go version

go version go1.27.0 darwin/arm64

### What did you do?

When using `encoding/json/v2` to marshal and unmarshal an instance of a type that contains an embedded field, if the type of the field implements marshal methods such as `encoding.TextAppender`, marshaling succeeds but unmarshaling fails. I find it confusing because the unmarshaling behavior is affected by a marshal method. The following is an example code snippet:

 [CODE_BLOCK] package main

import (
 "encoding"
 "encoding/json/v2"
 "fmt"
)

var _ encoding.TextAppender = (*Base)(nil)

type Base struct {
 ID string
}

func (b *Base) AppendText(buf []byte) ([]byte, error) {
 return append(buf, b.ID...), nil
}

type Container struct {
 Base
}

func main() {
 b := &Container{ID: "id_for_marshal"}
 if buf, err := json.Marshal(b); err != nil {
 fmt.Println("marshal error:", err)
 } else {
 fmt.Printf("marshal success: %s\n", buf)
 }

 b = new(Container)
 if err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(`{"ID":"id_for_unmarshal"}`), b); err != nil {
 fmt.Println("unmarshal error:", err)
 } else {
 fmt.Printf("unmarshal success: %#v\n", b)
 }
}
 [/CODE_BLOCK] 

### What did you see happen?

 [CODE_BLOCK] marshal success: "id_for_marshal"

unmarshal error: json: cannot unmarshal JSON object into Go main.Container: embedded Go struct field Base of type main.Base must not implement marshal or unmarshal methods
 [/CODE_BLOCK] 

### What did you expect to see?

- **Option 1 (most expected)**: Marshaling succeeds and unmarshaling succeeds.
 - Rationale: Marshal methods should not affect unmarshaling behavior.
- **Option 2**: Marshaling fails and unmarshaling fails.
 - Rationale: `encoding/json/v2` rejects all embedded fields of types that implement custom marshal or unmarshal methods.
- **Option 3**: Marshaling fails and unmarshaling succeeds.
 - Rationale: Similar to Option 2, but marshal methods only affect marshaling behavior.
